    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) and **Andy Pages** (74.42), both of whom benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Sugano. **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier play, as his projection surges due to a park factor boost and the opponent's high xERA of 4.93. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** (71.82) finds himself in a prime spot in the leadoff hole against Ober; the combination of a favorable matchup, strong xwOBA, and wind blowing out makes him a high-efficiency start that significantly outperforms his base projection.\n\nWhile the top of our lineup holds strong, the middle of the order presents tougher sledding against tough southpaws. **Gunnar Henderson** (52.61) and **Coby Mayo** (47.65) must contend with McClanahan, with **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score hampered by a harsh 15% platoon penalty. Consequently, the most difficult decision today was balancing the upside of our bench depth; however, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** currently without a game, the decision-making process was simplified by limited availability. **Sam Antonacci** (42.58) represents the lowest-scored starter in the lineup today, narrowly avoiding the bench despite a stiff 9% penalty for an L/L matchup against Imanaga, as we prioritize his roster depth over available alternatives.\n\nLooking ahead, we must closely monitor the status of **Jacob Wilson**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill**, all of whom are playing with \"Lineup Pending\" designations. If these assumed positions shift drastically, we risk losing the \"Order\" bonus points that currently buoy their daily efficiency scores. Should late scratches occur, we will need to re-evaluate our utility spot, though for now, the Waves are positioned to exploit the weak back-end of the opposing rotations while navigating the scarcity of stolen bases by leaning on the high-contact profiles of **Jacob Wilson** and **Luis Robert Jr.** to stabilize our 5x5 production.",
